+# Round 2 summary: John's findings and Nandini's Track B
+
+Branch `fix/ch-trackA` in `C:\ripple`, cut from `main` `4a8d820b`. Nothing is committed or pushed; review the diff, then commit by hand. The whole change (Track A and this round) is in `docs/audit/ripple-all-fixes.patch`.
+
+## What changed, in the order to review it
+
+1. **Server safety** (`backend/app/main.py`, `api/app_routes.py`, `records/repo.py`, `snapshot/builder.py`, `services/messages.py`, `Dockerfile`)
+   - Body size counted as it arrives; strict whole-number money; dates limited to 2000 to 2100.
+   - A pending cheque holds its amount on the bill; two cheques cannot pay the same money. Duplicate bill numbers refused; the forecast builder can no longer fail on two bills with the same number.
+   - Shared demo accounts cannot change the team or reset the shared business. Invite answers do not reveal who has an account.
+   - Stock cannot go below zero by adjustment. WhatsApp numbers carry the country code. `transactions.csv` has a byte-order mark and a formula guard on the party name.
+   - `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, real 404 status for unknown addresses, gzip for text, HSTS over HTTPS, share image address from `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`.
+2. **Screens** (`frontend/src/...`)
+   - Book > Ledger: Cleared and Bounced on pending cheques. Payment dialog, Add customer or supplier, "Can I take this order?": the shared input parsers and error handling. Set-up asks before replacing records.
+   - New pages: `/privacy`, `/terms`, a 404 page, a cookie notice, a title per screen. Settings no longer shifts when its data arrives.
+   - Colours, ARIA, focus and touch-size fixes; the main font is preloaded; smaller Tamil and Devanagari fonts.
+3. **Tests** (`tests/test_audit_round2.py`, `tests/test_trackB_fuzz.py`, `frontend/src/lib/*.test.ts`, `e2e/*.mjs`, `postman/`)
+4. **Evidence and reports** (`docs/audit/nandini/`, `docs/audit/chirantan/`)
+
+Generated files in the diff you can skim: `fixtures/simulation/examples/*.json` (regenerated by `generate_examples.py`), `frontend/public/*.png` (made by `e2e/make-share-images.mjs`), `postman/collections/ripple-api.json` (made by `postman/build_collection.py`), `e2e/package-lock.json`.
+
+## Decisions only you can make
+
+1. **Proxy hops.** How many proxies does Railway put in front of the app? Set `TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS` to that number (the rate limits depend on it).
+2. **The unmounted backend.** About 1,700 lines (10 routes, including `/demo/reset`) are never served. Delete or integrate?
+3. **John's branch.** `multilingual-speech-to-text` commits `node_modules`, `dist` and a database. May it be cleaned (source files only) before it is merged?
+4. **Unused routes.** 15 mounted routes have no caller in the screens. Three are real features without a screen (edit a party, create a bill, set a promised date). Add screens, or leave the routes?
+5. **The "ways to fix" terms** (2% discount, 90% advance, 1.5% fee, 10 days) are assumptions. Make them settings, or leave them for the demo?
+6. **Hindi and Tamil.** Only navigation, Today and Book are translated. Get a fluent reviewer, or say so on the screen?
+7. **Legal pages.** `/privacy` and `/terms` are plain-language summaries. Someone should check them (the DPDP Act, 2023) before real customer data is held.
+8. **Shared demo.** Its data is still writable by anyone who knows the documented password; only the team list and the reset are protected. "Load demo data" restores it.
+
+9. **Merging with John's files.** His report names `postman/collections/ripple-api.json`, `postman/build_collection.py`, `e2e/audit.mjs`, `docs/production-readiness-audit.md`, `docs/bug-ledger.md` and `tests/test_audit_regressions.py`. The first two have the same paths as this branch's collection and generator, so they will conflict. Keep one collection (this branch's has 261 requests covering Track A and Track B; John's has 198) or rename one before merging. His regression tests overlap these fixes: where both exist, keep both and let them agree.
+
+## What was not tested
+
+Firefox, Safari, a real phone, screen readers, the deployed site, the Docker build, a live AI model, the voice controls, load. Postman MCP and CLI were not available (Newman was used).
