+# Final report: Track B (Nandini), with the fixes for John's findings
+
+Name: Nandini (Track B), run together with the fixes for John's report (Track C findings that were present in this codebase). Branch: `fix/ch-trackA` in `C:\ripple`, cut from `main` `4a8d820b`.
+Branch state: **nothing committed or pushed.** The fixes are in the working tree and in `docs/audit/ripple-all-fixes.patch`. `main`, `bugbounty` and `redundant` do not contain them yet.
+
+1. **Frontend routes discovered and tested.** 9 app routes plus 3 public addresses added in this round (`/privacy`, `/terms`, the 404 page). Track B tested 14 route states at 1440 px and 12 at 390 px: Login, Privacy, Terms, 404, Set-up, Khata, Orders (sales, purchase, "Can I take this order?"), Inventory (raw, finished, recipes, movements), Settings. Plus the payment dialog, the party drawer and the reminder composer.
+2. **Controls.** 683 control observations. 1440 px: 345 = **PASS 307, PASS (explained) 13, NOT APPLICABLE 19, BLOCKED 6, FAIL 0.** 390 px: 338 = **PASS 266, PASS (explained) 12, NOT APPLICABLE 54, BLOCKED 6, FAIL 0.** The explained ones are controls the sweep cannot judge (a self-link, an empty-field submit stopped by the browser, a download, the 404 page, a button removed by an earlier click in the same run); each is listed with its reason in `ui-control-coverage.json`. The 6 blocked are destructive or session-ending (Remove x3, Load demo data, Log out, Log out everywhere) and are covered by journeys. Plus **65 journey checks, all PASS**, in Chrome and again in Edge (cancel and confirm for every destructive step).
+3. **Backend endpoints.** 87 route definitions: 77 mounted (30 GET, 32 POST, 4 PUT, 7 PATCH, 4 DELETE, including the new `/robots.txt` and `/sitemap.xml`), 10 not mounted. The Postman collection exercises 70 of the 77 mounted. Not in it: `logout-all` and `load-demo` (covered by journeys), the set-up and snapshot routes (they call an external AI service), `simulation/run` and `compare` (John's folder). 15 mounted routes have no caller in the screens; 3 are real features with no screen (edit a party, create a bill, set a promised date).
+4. **Postman MCP.** Not available in this session; no Postman tools were exposed. No remote workspace or collection was inspected.
+5. **Postman CLI.** Not installed. **Newman** was used instead, installed outside the repository. Local only; no Postman authentication.
+6. **Collection.** `postman/collections/ripple-api.json` (generated by `postman/build_collection.py` and `postman/trackB_folders.py`), 15 folders, **273 requests**. Track B folders: 08 Khata, 09 Invoices and payments, 10 Orders, 11 Inventory, 12 Settings/export/team/data, 13 Cross-business (two sandboxes), 14 Supervisor on Track B routes. Each write is read back; each folder removes what it created where the API allows.
+7. **Assertions.** Final run with the supervisor password supplied at run time: **273 requests, 413 assertions, 0 failed.** Without the password the 22 supervisor requests are skipped (251 run). The first runs found: a collection test that read the byte-order mark from decoded text (collection mistake), a delete that is correctly refused for a material with stock history (collection mistake), the owner's id read too late (collection mistake), folder order (supervisor folders now run last), and one real bug: money sent as the text `"100"` was accepted (B-019, fixed).
+8. **Browser errors and unexpected text.** No console error, page error, failed asset, HTTP error or unexpected browser dialog in the 65 journeys, in either browser. No `undefined`, `NaN`, `[object Object]` or stack trace on any screen. Defects found by other means: 55 contrast and ARIA violation groups (axe), layout shift on slow connections, uncompressed scripts, a relative favicon path.
+9. **Authentication and authorisation.** Not signed in: a visitor to any `/app` address is sent to sign-in. Every write route (all POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE routes) answers 403 `MISSING_CSRF_HEADER` without the header (test). Supervisor: 403 on parties, payments, invoices, exports, money rules, team, reset (15 requests); order, purchase, inventory and stock responses carry no `_paise` or rupee sign (Postman, journeys). Cross-business: another business's party, payment, edit, datasheet, order, purchase order, material, stock and team ids all return 404 (12 requests). **J-001 (High):** the shared demo accounts could remove each other, invite owners and reset the shared business. Fixed. **J-005:** rate limits behind a proxy fixed in code (A-003); the proxy count on the real host is not known.
+10. **Security findings by severity.** Critical: none. High (fixed): J-001 shared demo lock-out, J-004 two cheques paying one bill, B-001 a duplicate bill number breaking every forecast screen, B-002 extreme dates (HTTP 500 and a poisoned forecast). Medium (fixed): J-002 CSV formula, J-003 chunked body, J-006, B-003 negative stock, B-004, B-005, B-007, B-008, B-010 to B-013, B-021; J-005 open on the deployment side. Low and Info: the rest of `bug-ledger.md`. A schema-driven fuzz (71 routes, over 2,000 hostile bodies, ids and query values) finds no 500, no stack trace and no file path in any answer after the fixes.
+11. **AI, chatbot and speech-to-text.** Munim is Track A. For Track B: set-up with no AI key shows a plain message and keeps the typed text; "Load the demo business" and "Approve" now ask before replacing records. **Not tested:** the AI-backed set-up with a key, microphone dictation on the set-up page (headless Chrome has no audio).
+12. **Financial engine and database integrity.** Orders: every forward stage and back, purchase-order receive and undo, with stock moving and returning exactly, and the Risk and Finance "Books check" still passing after an undo (journeys 4 and 11). Fixed: pending cheques can no longer over-allocate a bill (J-004); stock cannot go below zero (B-003); two bills with one number no longer break the forecast (B-001); dates between 2000 and 2100 only (B-002); whole-number money only (B-019); `transactions.csv` encodes non-English names (B-009). Not tested here: migrations, concurrency, rollback (Track C).
+13. **Bugs fixed and files changed.** 31 of 34 ledger items fixed or added (see `bug-ledger.md`). Backend: `main.py`, `api/app_routes.py`, `records/repo.py`, `snapshot/builder.py`, `services/messages.py`, `services/fixes.py`, `Dockerfile`. Frontend: `index.html`, `App.tsx`, `main.tsx`, new `Legal.tsx`, `NotFound.tsx`, `CookieNotice.tsx`; `Book.tsx`, `Khata.tsx`, `Orders.tsx`, `Setup.tsx`, `Settings.tsx`, `Login.tsx`, `PaymentDialog.tsx`, `PartyDrawer.tsx`, `ui.tsx`, `NetworkView.tsx`, `lib/api.ts`, `lib/format.ts`, three style files; `services/api.ts` removed (unused). Also regenerated `fixtures/simulation/examples/*.json`, new share image and icons, README, `.env.example`.
+14. **Regression tests added and results.** Backend `unittest`: 26 in `tests/test_audit_round2.py` and 4 in `tests/test_trackB_fuzz.py`, all pass. Frontend `vitest`: 2 new tests (`whatsappNumber`) and 5 new error codes; 92 pass. Playwright: 65 journey checks (`e2e/regression-trackB.mjs`), plus `audit-a11y.mjs`, `audit-keyboard.mjs`, `audit-speed.mjs`, `audit-controls.mjs`. Postman: the collection above.
+15. **Build and type-check (actual).** `npx tsc -b`: 0 errors. `npx vitest run`: 92 passed. `npm run build`: built. `python -m unittest discover`: **188 tests OK, 1 skipped** (380 seconds, with nothing else running). An earlier run of the same suite failed once with "risk did not finish" while the machine was running browsers and Newman at the same time (the suite took 960 seconds); the test passes alone in 3 seconds and in the clean run. Axe-core: **0 violations in 80 scans** (16 pages and states x Night, Day, Lamp, and high contrast in two themes). Keyboard: 376 tab stops on 14 pages. Reflow: no horizontal scroll at 320, 360, 390, 768 px and at 720x450.
+16. **Unresolved defects and impact.** J-005 deployment: set `TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS` to the real number of proxies. B-023: only navigation, Today and Book are translated into Hindi and Tamil; the other screens show English there. B-024: no screen to edit a party, enter a bill or set a promised date. Page speed on a slow phone profile: largest paint 2.5 to 3.3 s (target 2.5 s). Everything open from Track A stays open (A-006, A-007, A-009 and the five decisions).
+17. **Blocked or untested.** Firefox, Safari and a real phone; screen readers (NVDA, VoiceOver); reduced-motion behaviour; the deployed site and its HTTPS behaviour; the Docker build; a live AI model; microphone dictation; load and 5,000-row behaviour; Lighthouse itself (the same metrics were read from the browser); Postman MCP and CLI.
+18. **Release-readiness recommendation (Track B scope).** **Fit for the demo and for peer testing.** Before a public deployment: set `TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS` and `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, have the privacy and terms text checked, translate the remaining screens or say so on screen, and run a screen reader and a real phone over Khata, Orders and the payment dialog. No Critical finding is open. This is evidence of what was tested, not proof that no defect remains.
+
+## Decisions I need from you
+
+See `docs/audit/ROUND2-SUMMARY.md`: proxy hops; the unmounted backend; cleaning John's branch; the 15 unused routes (3 real features without a screen); the "ways to fix" terms; Hindi and Tamil review; legal wording; the shared demo's writable data; and the file conflicts with John's collection and generator.
